(text
"Primary protection per cell: OV 4.25V / UV 3.00V; inhibit 0V-cell recharge. Charge/discharge overcurrent use VM and actual series resistance.\nQ601/Q602 are common-DRAIN NMOS. Q603/Q604 are common-SOURCE PMOS; no body-diode bypass when OFF.\nRUN typical falling cutoff ~6.63V, restart ~6.72V, OV cutoff ~8.6V. USB clamps RUN_BASE independently of MCU.\nRaw B- returns only to protection/balance circuits. USB, charger, NTC and EEG use protected GND.\nHardware power-off is NOT galvanic or patient isolation. Remove electrodes before inserting USB."
